# BMW 5 Series E28 four-door saloon, 1981-1987.
#
# The second 5-series: a squarer, larger development of the E12 on the same
# three-box layout, with the low waistline and thin pillars of the early 1980s.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_5_Series_(E28)
#
# Dimensions 4.620 x 1.700 x 1.415 m, wheelbase 2.625 m, from the English
# Wikipedia dimension box. Mirrors and rubbing strips take the modelled width
# past the body figure.
#
# Colours. A UK colour card for the E28 was not located; the research for this
# model found only aftermarket paint-code lists, which do not establish UK
# availability. The four names below are BMW programme colours of the period
# from the E21 paint register (BMWE21.net), which reproduces the 1978/79 and
# 1980-on brochure colour pages, and each is documented as offered inside the
# E28's production years:
#   Polaris metallic  060, offered 1975-1984
#   Saphirblau meta.  149, offered 1980-1984
#   Hennarot          052, offered 1980-1984
#   Schwarz           086, offered 1975-1982
# This is recorded as period BMW palette evidence, not as proof of UK
# availability, which the research could not establish either way.
# Weights silver 3, red 3, blue 2, black 2, total 10, provisional pending the
# central rebase.
#
# Speed 205 km/h, below the 535i's 225 km/h and above the four-cylinder cars,
# for the volume UK six-cylinder models. Comfort 115/503, on the line
# 330 + 1.5 x 115, the same as the E36. Classes 2,3.
#
# Dates are road presence, not production: September 1981 intro, retires
# staggered 1999-2002 on an eighteen- to twenty-one-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-e28.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-e28.dae (53 objects). References:
# citycars/references/bmw-e28/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the corners are
# simplified and the rubbing strips carry slightly proud of the body. The
# profile photograph's apparent wheelbase/length ratio is 0.567 against the
# published 0.571; perspective prevents treating that as a dimensional
# contradiction, and the published dimensions were kept.

obj=citycar
name=BMW5E28(PolarisSilver)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=1981
intro_month=9
retire_year=2002
retire_month=6
speed=205
length=3
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=115
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=503

